    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211-a2">

                <pb facs="0271" n="221" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg221"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 180.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eustis to Mr. Hanotaux.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June 25,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your excellency’s dispatch of this morning informing me of the assassination
                    of the President of the Republic. Without awaiting the instructions of my
                    Government, I hasten to give you the assurance that the dreadful misfortune
                    which, in the person of its first magistrate, befalls the old and faithful ally
                    of the United States will awaken in all American hearts a feeling of profound
                    emotion.</p>
                <pb facs="0272" n="222" xml:id="pg222"/>
                <p>I beg you, Mr. Minister, to convey to Madame Carnot the expression of my
                    respectful condolence, and to rest assured that in the painful trial through
                    which France is now passing and with her the democratic institutions she so
                    worthily represents in the old world, the sympathies of my fellow citizens, as
                    well as those of my Government, will not cease to accompany her.</p>
                <p>I take, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Eustis.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
